 "result_text": "I fixed `manage_addZSearch` in `src/Shared/DC/ZRDB/Search.py`, which was raising `TypeError: object of type 'map' has no len()` on Python 3. I only checked that the module imports. I didn't run the tests or try the ZMI form.\n\nThere were two bugs:\n- **The crash:** `qs` was built with `map(...)`, and the code then called `len(qs)` on it. I replaced it with a list comprehension.\n- **A second bug on the same path:** the report generation used `map(_report(q, report_style), qs)`. That calls `_report` once and then maps its string result over `qs`, which would have failed next. It now builds the report with `_report(q, report_style) for q in qs`, once for DTML methods and once for page templates.\n\nI left the other `map(...)` calls in the file alone because `join` consumes them directly. I didn't change any tests or commit anything.",
